 ### [RLE4 Compression](4441-rle4-compression.md)
-RLE4 Compression converts a dense 3D voxel grid into a sparse, column-oriented structure called **Map4** to solve memory bloat in large volumes with significant empty space. It processes the volume slice-by-slice (XZ planes), encoding runs of empty space (skip) and occupied space (solid) along the Y-axis into 16-bit words, while storing per-voxel color and intensity data in a separate texture buffer. Unlike Binary Voxel RLE Encoding which stores binary occupancy, RLE4 preserves per-voxel material and intensity information for splatting. It differs from Run-length encoded voxel runs by using a fixed 16-bit RLE format with specific bit-widths for solid (6 bits) and skip (10 bits) runs, and by including a perturbation step for surface normals.#### RLE Export
-Compresses the voxel grid using Run-Length Encoding and saves it to a binary file.
